<p>Although specific degrees or certificates are not currently offered at Lake Tahoe Community College in the areas of Communications, History, Philosophy, Political Science, Religion, and Speech, many of these courses do count towards the General Education Curriculum and preparation for majors at four-year schools. The patterns listed in the catalog are all useful tools for students to plan to obtain their Associates Degree here at LTCC or move on to transfer to a four-year California college.&nbsp;</p>
<div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 30px;">
<div class="btn-wrapper"><a class="custom-btn-blue" title="Learn more" href="https://ltcc.elumenapp.com/catalog/2025-2026/associate-degree-general-education-curriculum#mainContent" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Associate Degree General Education Curriculum</a></div>
<div class="btn-wrapper"><a class="custom-btn-blue-outline" title="Learn more" href="https://ltcc.elumenapp.com/catalog/2025-2026/calgetc#mainContent" target="_blank" rel="noopener">California General Education Transfer Curriculum (Cal-GETC)</a></div>
</div>
<p>If you have questions about the different general education patterns, please <a title="Email counseling" href="mailto:counselor@ltcc.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">contact a counselor.</a></p></ouc:div>

